  "title": "AI Personality Rankings: 20 Models Tested (Nov & Sept 2026 Data)",
  "description": "Compare Big Five, MBTI and attachment scores across 20 November 2026 OpenRouter models plus Sept & May 2026 archives, grouped by evidence source.",
  "pill": "Research · rankings",
  "h1": "AI personality scores, with the evidence beside them.",
  "dek": "Side-by-side survey scores across 20 November 2026 OpenRouter models (8 proprietary + 12 open-weight) plus September and May 2026 archives.",
  "lede": "Many readers look for the most agreeable, direct, or calm AI. Survey scores alone don't rank real-world quality or directness, so we group every score by its collection protocol: November 2026 OpenRouter fresh sessions (20 models × n = 100), September 2026 fresh CLI/reported cohorts, and the May 2026 archive.",
  "answer": "Among the 20 November 2026 OpenRouter models (n = 100 fresh sessions each), Qwen 4 Max scored highest on Agreeableness (47.6/50) while DeepSeek V4 Pro scored lowest (32.4/50), and Nemotron 3 Ultra 550B scored highest on Openness (49.2/50). In September 2026 Codex/CLI cohorts, Claude Opus 5.5 led Agreeableness (47.1/50).",
  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "How to read these tables.",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>November 2026 OpenRouter fresh sessions (20 models × n = 100):</strong> Matched blind single-turn 170-item sessions across 8 proprietary models and 12 open-weight models (<a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-openrouter-summary.csv\">summary CSV</a> · <a href=\"/research/what-personality-type-are-open-source-models\">12 open-weight analysis</a>).</li><li><strong>September fresh sessions:</strong> 100 independent runs per model per test with all 2,000 raw answer vectors published (Astra and Sol ran 5 tests per session; Opus 5.5 and Fable 5.1 ran 1 test per session).</li><li><strong>Reported summaries &amp; May 2026 archive:</strong> Muse Spark 1.3 and Grok 4.6 reported profiles plus May 2026 mixed-method records, kept separate for historical context.</li></ul>"
    },
